WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.652
This slide shows four columns that could all be stored as integers.

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:08.602
Heart rate is a measurement recorded to whole units.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:10.562
Emergency visits is a count.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:12.707
Patient ID is a label.

00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:16.952
Satisfaction is ordinal. The same technical dtype supports four different analytical meanings.

00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:21.367
This is why the correct question is not, what dtype does pandas show?

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:26.572
The correct question is, how was this value generated and what comparisons make sense?

00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:32.452
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:32.452 --> 00:00:37.662
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:44.622
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:44.622 --> 00:00:49.477
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:54.640
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
